      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T20:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding the -n saves about 30s on one of my repos, and makes a NOOP go down to 6ms! It turns out that git update-server-info is expense when you have ~2Mrefs. Updating the server info is only useful for the http dumb protocol. Does Gerrit even support that?",
      "revId": "eeaaae5f15b06adf242f1327383465924cb67352",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a326536a_de0367e8",
        "filename": "contrib/hooks/ref-updated_repack-geometric.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T20:09:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like git should be fixed for this case, more info here: https://lore.kernel.org/git/LV8PR12MB9407CB282D1FD4998C659D29C2442@LV8PR12MB9407.namprd12.prod.outlook.com/T/#u",
      "parentUuid": "40220918_10e8f7db",
      "revId": "eeaaae5f15b06adf242f1327383465924cb67352",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3726e60_c4be6524",
        "filename": "contrib/hooks/ref-updated_repack-geometric.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T20:36:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch. That\u0027s an odd default, I don\u0027t think the dumb http protocol is still widely used.\n\nIf you set `gc.packRefs\u003dfalse` then git gc and git repack don\u0027t pack refs.\nSee https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config#Documentation/git-config.txt-gcpackRefs",
      "parentUuid": "a326536a_de0367e8",
      "revId": "eeaaae5f15b06adf242f1327383465924cb67352",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a8ba76a_ed9074f0",
        "filename": "contrib/hooks/ref-updated_repack-geometric.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T20:56:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, even with -c gc.packRefs\u003dfalse added to the git repack command, it still tries to update-server-info for refs (I don\u0027t believe is is repacking them, it is just updating the file for http dumb protocol). I suspect that this file cannot be used with ACLs, so Gerrit likely doesn\u0027t even support the http dumb protocol?",
      "parentUuid": "a3726e60_c4be6524",
      "revId": "eeaaae5f15b06adf242f1327383465924cb67352",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13669ed3_75caf2f8",
        "filename": "contrib/hooks/ref-updated_repack-geometric.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 104,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T21:44:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The dumb protocol doesn\u0027t need a git server but just a web server. It only supports read (fetch, clone) but no write (push).\n\nInstead of dynamic negotiation between git client and the web server there is just a static info/refs file which the client can download using an HTTP GET request to discover the refs the dumb server has. This file is written by the update-server-info command (or repack as you found out). This means whenever a ref changes this file needs to be recomputed which is clearly a lot of overhead if there are many refs (like in Gerrit). See https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Transfer-Protocols\n\nJGit client supports the dumb protocol, see https://github.com/eclipse-jgit/jgit/blob/master/org.eclipse.jgit.http.test/tst/org/eclipse/jgit/http/test/DumbClientDumbServerTest.java\n\nI don\u0027t know anyone using this ancient protocol.",
      "parentUuid": "4a8ba76a_ed9074f0",
      "revId": "eeaaae5f15b06adf242f1327383465924cb67352",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
